\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Chip noticed. Dr Quark was reading something on his tablet and either didn\'92t notice or had assigned the matter no scientific significance.\
Eloise came around her desk and took the remaining chair.\
\'93Sarah is on stress leave,\'94 Johnny began.\
\'93I know where Sarah is.\'94\
Johnny nodded as if they had agreed on something.\
Eloise looked to Quark. \'93Do we have evidence that Project Kebab caused the Gibson Desert earthquake?\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
Chip shifted heavily in his chair.\
\'93Do we have evidence that it didn\'92t?\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
\'93Thank you.\'94\
\'93That doesn\'92t make those statements equal,\'94 Quark added.\
Johnny stopped nodding.\
Chip leaned forward. \'93The earthquake happened at the same time, in a place the geometry says it shouldn\'92t have known existed.\'94\
\'93I\'92ve seen the correlation,\'94 Quark said.\
\'93And?\'94\
\'93And it\'92s a correlation.\'94\
Chip slapped a hand on his knee. \'93You academics would wait for a second bullet before you agreed the first one killed someone.\'94\
Quark looked over his glasses. \'93Do you have evidence I haven\'92t seen?\'94\
Chip stared at him.\
\'93You know I can\'92t show you.\'94\
Quark returned to his tablet.\
Johnny brightened. \'93Exactly.\'94\
Quark looked up again. \'93No, Mr Stoat. You don\'92t get to borrow my argument.\'94\
Johnny\'92s brightness went away.\
Chip pointed at him anyway. \'93He wants to keep pushing because every time the machine doesn\'92t explode under his feet he thinks he\'92s invented safety.\'94\
\'93That\'92s not fair,\'94 Johnny complained. \'93Sometimes it explodes somewhere else.\'94\
Nobody laughed.\
Johnny looked annoyed with them.\
Eloise folded her hands. \'93Mr Stockwell, what exactly are you recommending?\'94\
\'93Stop.\'94\
\'93For how long?\'94\
Chip hesitated.\
\'93Until you understand what you\'92re doing.\'94\
Johnny groaned. \'93That could take centuries.\'94\
\'93Particularly with you involved.\'94\
\'93Here we go.\'94\
\'93No,\'94 Eloise said.\
Both men stopped.\
She looked at Chip. \'93You were brought into Project Kebab because you had experience nobody else here possessed.\'94\
\'93Correct.\'94\
\'93You have repeatedly warned us of dangers you cannot substantiate.\'94\
\'93Cannot reveal.\'94\
\'93The distinction is becoming expensive.\'94\
Chip\'92s face darkened.\
\'93You think I\'92m making it up?\'94\
Eloise glanced at Quark.\
Quark kept his attention on his tablet.\
Chip saw that too.\
Johnny sank back into his chair with the pleasure of a child watching another child being sent to the principal.\
\'93You\'92ve got no one left backing you,\'94 he said.\
Chip turned on him.\
Johnny\'92s chair moved backwards a few centimetres.\
Eloise looked at Johnny. \'93That was unnecessary.\'94\
Johnny busied himself adjusting his cuff.\
Chip stood.\
The movement put Johnny another few centimetres away.\
\'93I\'92m telling you the machine is dangerous.\'94\
\'93You\'92ve told us,\'94 Eloise said.\
\'93I\'92m telling you to stop.\'94\
\'93And I\'92ve heard you.\'94\
Chip remained standing.\
\'93What happens when you don\'92t?\'94\
Eloise waited.\
Chip looked at Quark, then Johnny, then back to Eloise.\
\'93I get in the way.\'94\
Johnny snorted.\
Chip looked at him.\
Johnny stopped.\
Eloise touched her desk.\
The office door opened.\
Two security people entered.\
Johnny sat upright. \'93Hang on.\'94\
Nobody had asked him anything.\
Chip looked at Eloise and gave a low laugh.\
\'93So that\'92s it.\'94\
\'93You\'92ve made your position admirably clear.\'94\
\'93I was hired to stop you doing something stupid.\'94\
\'93And now?\'94\
\'93I\'92m doing my job.\'94\
Eloise nodded to security.\
Johnny looked suddenly uncomfortable. \'93I only meant he shouldn\'92t be making decisions.\'94\
Eloise ignored him.\
Chip allowed the guards to approach.\
\'93Where?\'94 one asked.\
Eloise considered Chip for a moment.\
\'93The brig.\'94\
Chip\'92s eyebrows lifted.\
Johnny looked at the floor.\
Quark finally put his tablet down.\
Chip turned for the door with the guards.\
\'93You kept Sarah down there,\'94 he said.\
\'93And Kathy and Hayley.\'94\
Chip grunted. \'93Good company.\'94\
The door closed behind him.\
For several seconds nobody spoke.\
Eloise looked at Johnny.\
Whatever satisfaction he\'92d been feeling had gone somewhere safer.\
